@startuml implementation-review
!include state-machine-style.iuml
title Slop Machine | Implementation, validation and senior review

state "Verify mounted clone before code\nSee project-workspace.puml: verify_for_code\nAccepted spec; current or reconciled saved code" as Prepare
state "Select implementer session\nSee role-session.puml: select_for_pass\nrole = implementer; explicit task + feedback" as ISession
state "Implement / repair\nBounded assignment" as Implement
state "Capture immutable candidate\nCode snapshot + criterion mapping\nFinding responses + limitations" as Snapshot
state "Run configured validation\nBind results to candidate snapshot" as Validate
state "Select reviewer session\nSee role-session.puml: select_for_pass\nrole = reviewer; original spec, design, code, checks" as RSession
state "Senior engineering review\nCorrectness, scope, design alignment\nEvidence and unresolved findings" as Review
state "Evaluate significant agent output\nPlans, completion result + reviewer findings\nSee output-handoff-policy.puml" as OutputPolicy
state ReviewOutcome <<choice>>
state "Record actionable feedback\nStable finding IDs + evidence\nNo silent requirement changes" as Feedback
state "Repair gate\nBudget + scope + progress checks" as RepairGate
state "Final approval gate\nExact snapshot; current spec/policy\nAll required checks + no blocking findings" as Approve
state "Ready for publication" as Ready <<success>>
state "Scope blocker\nPropose separate bounded work" as ScopeBlock <<blocked>>
state "Needs attention\nClarification, no progress, or limits" as Attention <<attention>>
state "Repeat preflight\nWorkspace target or task inputs changed" as Recheck <<attention>>

[*] --> Prepare
Prepare --> ISession : workspace and context ready
Prepare --> Recheck : return recheck_preflight
Prepare --> Attention : workspace not safely prepared
ISession --> Implement : assignment accepted; policy allows
ISession --> Attention : session selection or context handoff failed
ISession --> ScopeBlock : outbound handoff found necessary extra work
Implement --> OutputPolicy : significant plan or completion proposed
Implement --> Attention : ambiguous requirements
OutputPolicy --> Implement : allowed intermediate plan/continuation
OutputPolicy --> Snapshot : allowed implementation completion
OutputPolicy --> ReviewOutcome : allowed senior review result
OutputPolicy --> Feedback : [implementer; rejected proposal]\nbounded in-scope correction
OutputPolicy --> RSession : [reviewer; rejected result]\nbounded corrected review pass
OutputPolicy --> ScopeBlock : necessary extra work confirmed
OutputPolicy --> Attention : uncertain scope, policy failure\nor uncontained effects
Snapshot --> Validate : snapshot complete
Validate --> RSession : required checks passed
Validate --> Feedback : application check failed\n/ attach validation evidence
RSession --> Review : assignment accepted; policy allows
RSession --> Attention : session selection or context handoff failed
RSession --> ScopeBlock : outbound handoff found necessary extra work
Review --> OutputPolicy : structured review result/handoff proposed
ReviewOutcome --> Feedback : [changes_requested]
ReviewOutcome --> ScopeBlock : [scope_blocked]
ReviewOutcome --> Attention : [clarification_required]
ReviewOutcome --> Approve : [approved]
Feedback --> RepairGate
RepairGate --> Prepare : allowed, in scope, progress possible\n/ new repair assignment + iteration
RepairGate --> ScopeBlock : necessary extra work confirmed
RepairGate --> Attention : limits exhausted, disputed scope,\nor repeated unresolved failures
Approve --> Ready : checks and approval match same code/spec
Approve --> Snapshot : code/evidence changed / invalidate approval
Approve --> Attention : spec/policy conflict needs reassessment
Ready --> [*] : return approved snapshot
ScopeBlock --> [*] : return scope_blocked
Attention --> [*] : return attention
Recheck --> [*] : return recheck_preflight

note left of ISession
  role-session.puml owns fresh/reuse selection,
  explicit context delivery and session retirement.
  Lifecycle cleanup invokes its end_run path for both roles.
  Check failures and review repairs each re-enter selection.
end note
note right of Validate
  A test failure can require code repair.
  A failed test runner, malformed response, or
  provider outage is an operational failure:
  reconcile/retry under operation-guardrails.puml.
  Never label an infrastructure error a test pass.
end note
note right of Review
  Agents exchange typed JSON handoffs through
  the workflow; actual messages remain inspectable.
  Ponytail is configured per role; Caveman optional.
  Optimization cannot remove necessary evidence.
end note
note bottom of RepairGate
  Budget and cancellation checks apply before EVERY new assignment/check.
  Policy blocking can interrupt any protected action; it cannot silently pass.
  Global cancellation and unrecoverable errors return to lifecycle cleanup.
end note
@enduml
